    "description": "Various Minerals and Fossils\n9.6 lb Specimen Collection Lot\nGeodes, Teeth, and Tumbled Stones\nAssorted Dimensions\nUnsigned\nThis comprehensive geological collection features a diverse array of specimens ranging from large natural geodes to prehistoric marine fossils. The centerpiece of the lot includes two significant quartz geodes with well-defined crystalline interiors. Additionally, the collection includes three authentic Mosasaurus teeth recovered from Morocco, presented in a specialized display case with educational text regarding the Late Cretaceous marine reptile. The variety of colors and textures makes this an ideal starter set for a young collector or a significant addition to an existing mineral display.\nTwo large hollow geodes featuring dense white quartz crystal formations, measuring approximately 5-6 inches each\nThree fossilized Mosasaurus teeth in original display case from Morocco, dating to the Late Cretaceous period\nWide variety of mineral specimens including Amethyst, Pyrite (Fool's Gold), Jasper, Tiger's Eye, and Calcite\nLarge hand-knapped obsidian arrowhead and additional small stone points included for historical context\nCondition:\nThe collection is in good overall condition. Geodes remain structurally sound with intact crystalline structures and minimal exterior wear. Mineral specimens show natural variations, inclusions, and textures consistent with geological formations. The Mosasaurus display case is clean and legible. Tumbled and raw stones are clean and ready for display or lapidary use.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
